Assignment 2. DOM-based To-Do List 
• Aim: To build a dynamic, interactive To-Do List application using vanilla HTML, 
CSS, and JavaScript DOM manipulation. 
• Learning Objectives: Understand Document Object Model (DOM) selection 
methods, event listeners (click, submit), and dynamic element creation/deletion. 
• Theoretical Background: The DOM tree representing the page structure; using 
document.getElementById(), document.createElement(), appendChild(), and 
addEventListener() to modify UI state dynamically. 
• Detailed Requirements: 
o HTML Structure: An input text field, an "Add Task" button, and an 
empty list container (<ul> or <div>). 
o CSS Styling: Basic clean interface styling, including a visual indicator 
(like a strikethrough or color change) for completed tasks. 
o JavaScript Logic: 
▪ Add: Read the input field, create a new list item (<li>) 
dynamically, and append it to the container. 
▪ Toggle Complete: Click on a task to toggle a CSS class (e.g., 
.completed) that visually marks it off. 
▪ Delete: Add a "Delete" button next to each task that removes that 
specific node from the DOM when clicked.
